  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "round-heads-sahara-s016-p00156",
      "source_en": "With the exception of one date from the Acacus, we have no dating evidence for kettles or cupules. Two kettles at Uan Muhuggiag shelter in the Acacus were covered by a layer dated at 7,438+220 BP (calBP 8,255±209) which is the ante quem date for these kettles (Mori 2000). As mentioned before, Striedter, Tauveron and Ferhat (2002-3) propose the dating of the Algerian Tadrart kettles to at least the Late Pleistocene.",
